# ============================================================================
# SECTION 8: DEPLOYMENT & OPERATIONS GUIDE
# ============================================================================
#
# 8.1 System Requirements
# ----------------------------------------
#   - Python: 3.9+ (recommended: 3.11+)
#   - Memory: 512MB minimum, 2GB recommended
#   - CPU: 2 cores minimum, 4+ recommended
#   - Disk: 100MB for installation, 1GB for data
#   - OS: Linux (Ubuntu 20.04+), macOS (12+), Windows (10+)
#
# 8.2 Installation Steps
# ----------------------------------------
#   1. Clone the repository
#      git clone https://github.com/scarab/algorithm.git
#   2. Create virtual environment
#      python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
#   3. Install dependencies
#      pip install -r requirements.txt
#   4. Run verification
#      python scarab_algorithm.py
#   5. Verify all 320 demos pass
#
# 8.3 Production Deployment
# ----------------------------------------
#   - Use gunicorn or uvicorn for ASGI serving
#   - Configure reverse proxy (nginx/caddy) for TLS
#   - Set up monitoring with Prometheus + Grafana
#   - Configure log shipping to centralized logging
#   - Enable audit trail for compliance
#   - Set up alerting via IncidentManager
#   - Configure heartbeat monitoring for all services
#   - Set up automated backups for data stores
#
# 8.4 Scaling Guide
# ----------------------------------------
#   Horizontal Scaling:
#   - Deploy multiple instances behind LoadBalancer
#   - Use ConsistentHash for data distribution
#   - Configure PubSubBroker for cross-instance messaging
#   - Set up SessionHandler with shared store
#
#   Vertical Scaling:
#   - Increase CacheSystem capacity for hot data
#   - Tune BTree page size for I/O optimization
#   - Adjust ConnectionPool size for throughput
#   - Configure batch sizes for bulk operations
#
# 8.5 Monitoring Checklist
# ----------------------------------------
#   [ ] Heartbeat monitoring active for all services
#   [ ] TelemetryCollector receiving from all sources
#   [ ] AuditTrail enabled and retention configured
#   [ ] IncidentManager escalation rules configured
#   [ ] PermissionGuard RBAC policies reviewed
#   [ ] TokenVault rotation schedule active
#   [ ] CircuitBreaker thresholds tuned
#   [ ] RateLimiter quotas configured
#   [ ] LoadBalancer health checks passing
#   [ ] Backup verification schedule active
#
# ============================================================================
# SECTION 9: TROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE
# ============================================================================
#
# Problem: High CPU Usage
# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
#   1. Check CronScheduler for tight interval schedules
#   2. Review PageRanker iteration count (reduce if >50)
#   3. Verify FullTextIndex document count isn't excessive
#   4. Check for tight loops in EventStream consumers
#   5. Profile with TelemetryCollector CPU metrics
#   6. Review batch sizes in BulkProcessor
#   7. Check garbage collection frequency
#
# Problem: High Memory Usage
# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
#   1. Check CacheSystem capacity and eviction settings
#   2. Review EventStream max_size configuration
#   3. Verify AuditTrail max_entries limit
#   4. Check BloomFilter expected_items vs actual
#   5. Review DocumentStore index memory
#   6. Check for memory leaks in WeakRefRegistry
#   7. Monitor TelemetryCollector buffer sizes
#
# Problem: Slow Response Times
# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
#   1. Check ConnectionPool exhaustion (increase pool size)
#   2. Review CircuitBreaker state (may be half-open)
#   3. Verify LoadBalancer backend health
#   4. Check RateLimiter isn't throttling legitimate traffic
#   5. Review FullTextIndex search complexity
#   6. Check DataPipeline stage bottlenecks
#   7. Profile with TelemetryCollector latency metrics
#
# Problem: Authentication Failures
# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
#   1. Verify TokenVault token hasn't expired
#   2. Check if token was revoked (TokenVault.validate)
#   3. Review PermissionGuard role assignments
#   4. Check AuditTrail for failed auth attempts
#   5. Verify RBAC policies are correctly configured
#   6. Check token rotation schedule
#   7. Review session TTL configuration
#
# Problem: Data Inconsistencies
# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
#   1. Check for concurrent modification conflicts
#   2. Review EventSourcer event ordering
#   3. Verify ConsistentHash ring stability
#   4. Check DataSync conflict resolution settings
#   5. Review transaction boundaries in SagaOrchestrator
#   6. Verify snapshot integrity in data stores
#   7. Check SchemaRegistry version compatibility
#
# Problem: Service Communication Failures
# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
#   1. Check Heartbeat status for target services
#   2. Review CircuitBreaker state
#   3. Verify ServiceDiscovery registration TTL
#   4. Check DNS resolution with DNSResolver
#   5. Review TLS certificate expiration (CertManager)
#   6. Check proxy configuration (ProxyServer)
#   7. Verify webhook delivery status (WebhookManager)
#
# ============================================================================
# SECTION 10: GLOSSARY
# ============================================================================
#
#   Automaton
#     A self-operating machine or mechanism, here a cellular automaton for pattern evolution
#
#   B-Tree
#     A self-balancing tree data structure maintaining sorted data for efficient operations
#
#   Bloom Filter
#     A space-efficient probabilistic data structure for testing set membership
#
#   ChVS
#     Chromatic-Voicing-Sticking: the three-axis model for drumming technique
#
#   Circuit Breaker
#     A design pattern that prevents cascading failures in distributed systems
#
#   Consistent Hashing
#     A distributed hashing scheme for minimal key redistribution on node changes
#
#   CRUD
#     Create, Read, Update, Delete: basic data persistence operations
#
#   Damping Factor
#     In PageRank, the probability of following a link vs random jump (typically 0.85)
#
#   Event Sourcing
#     A pattern where state changes are stored as a sequence of events
#
#   Gearbox
#     The ChVS processing unit that maps chromatic patterns to sticking sequences
#
#   Heartbeat
#     A periodic signal sent by a service to indicate it is alive and healthy
#
#   Idempotent
#     An operation that produces the same result regardless of how many times it's applied
#
#   Inverted Index
#     A mapping from content (terms) to locations (documents) for full-text search
#
#   Match-Stick
#     The automaton model used for rule-based pattern generation
#
#   MVCC
#     Multi-Version Concurrency Control: concurrent access without locking
#
#   PageRank
#     An algorithm that ranks nodes by the structure of incoming links
#
#   PubSub
#     Publish-Subscribe: a messaging pattern decoupling producers from consumers
#
#   RBAC
#     Role-Based Access Control: permission management through role assignment
#
#   Saga
#     A pattern for managing distributed transactions through compensating actions
#
#   Scarab
#     The core algorithm engine, inspired by the scarab beetle's movement patterns
#
#   Skip List
#     A probabilistic data structure allowing O(log n) search within an ordered sequence
#
#   Sphere
#     One of four geometric spheres whose intersections define movement patterns
#
#   TF-IDF
#     Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency: a text relevance scoring method
#
#   Trie
#     A tree structure for storing strings where each node represents a character
#
#   TTL
#     Time To Live: the duration an item remains valid before expiration
#
#   WAL
#     Write-Ahead Log: a technique for ensuring data durability and crash recovery
#
# ============================================================================
# END OF COMPREHENSIVE DOCUMENTATION
