# ============================================================================
# SECTION 17: WIRE PROTOCOL SPECIFICATIONS
# ============================================================================
#
#
# === Event Bus Protocol ===
#
#   Message Format: JSON over internal message channel
#     {
#       'type': 'event',
#       'topic': '<topic_name>',
#       'payload': { ... },
#       'metadata': {
#         'id': '<uuid>',
#         'timestamp': '<iso8601>',
#         'source': '<component_id>',
#         'correlation_id': '<uuid>',
#         'causation_id': '<uuid>'
#       }
#     }
#
#   Topics: Dot-separated hierarchy (e.g., 'system.health.check')
#   Wildcards: '*' matches one level, '#' matches multiple levels
#   Delivery: At-least-once with idempotency key deduplication
#   Ordering: Per-partition ordering within a single publisher
#   Backpressure: Configurable buffer with drop-oldest policy
#
#
# === PubSub Protocol ===
#
#   Message Format:
#     {
#       'id': <int>,
#       'topic': '<topic>',
#       'body': <any>,
#       'published_at': <tick>
#     }
#
#   Subscribe: subscriber_id + topic -> registered
#   Publish: topic + message -> delivered to all subscribers
#   Receive: subscriber_id + limit -> messages from inbox
#   Unsubscribe: subscriber_id + topic -> removed
#   Topic lifecycle: auto-create on first publish, explicit delete
#   Message retention: until consumed or topic deleted
#   Delivery guarantee: at-most-once (fire and forget to inbox)
#
#
# === Heartbeat Protocol ===
#
#   Beat Format:
#     {
#       'service_id': '<string>',
#       'tick': <int>,
#       'status': 'healthy' | 'unhealthy' | 'unknown'
#     }
#
#   Registration: service_id + optional metadata
#   Beat: service_id -> last_beat updated, status -> healthy
#   Timeout: if (current_tick - last_beat) > timeout -> unhealthy
#   Recovery: next beat after timeout -> status restored to healthy
#   Metrics: beat_count, missed_count per service
#   Status: healthy (beats on time), unhealthy (missed), unknown (no beats)
#
#
# === Token Protocol ===
#
#   Token Format: 'tok_NNNNNN' (6-digit zero-padded)
#
#   Generate:
#     Input: owner (str), ttl (int), metadata (dict)
#     Output: token_id (str)
#
#   Validate:
#     Input: token_id (str)
#     Output: { valid: bool, owner?: str, reason?: str }
#     Reasons: 'revoked', 'not_found'
#
#   Revoke:
#     Input: token_id (str)
#     Output: bool (success)
#
#   Rotate:
#     Input: token_id (str)
#     Output: new_token_id (str) or None
#     Side effect: old token revoked
#
#
# === Audit Protocol ===
#
#   Entry Format:
#     {
#       'seq': <int>,
#       'actor': '<user_id>',
#       'action': '<action_type>',
#       'resource': '<resource_id>',
#       'details': { ... }
#     }
#
#   Log: actor + action + resource + details -> seq number
#   Query: optional filters (actor, action, resource) + limit
#   Count: optional filters (actor, action) -> int
#   Recent: n -> last n entries
#   Retention: max_entries with FIFO eviction
#
#
# === Incident Protocol ===
#
#   Incident ID Format: 'INC-NNNN' (4-digit zero-padded)
#
#   Lifecycle:
#     open -> investigating -> mitigated -> resolved -> closed
#
#   Create:
#     Input: title, severity (low|medium|high|critical), description
#     Output: inc_id
#
#   Assign: inc_id + assignee -> timeline entry
#   Update Status: inc_id + status -> timeline entry
#   Resolve: inc_id + resolution -> timeline entry, status -> resolved
#
#   Timeline: append-only list of actions with metadata
#   Severity levels: low < medium < high < critical
#   Statistics: total, by severity, open count
#
#
# === Job Protocol ===
#
#   Job Lifecycle: pending -> running -> completed | failed | cancelled
#
#   Submit:
#     Input: job_id, func, *args, **kwargs
#     Output: job_id
#     State: pending
#
#   Run:
#     Retry loop: up to max_retries attempts
#     On success: state -> completed, result stored
#     On failure: state -> failed, error stored
#
#   Cancel:
#     Only from pending state
#     State: pending -> cancelled
#
#   History: ordered list of {job_id, status, attempts}
#
#
# === Cron Protocol ===
#
#   Schedule Format:
#     {
#       'name': '<string>',
#       'interval': <int> (ticks between runs),
#       'func': <callable>,
#       'active': <bool>,
#       'last_run': <int | None>,
#       'run_count': <int>
#     }
#
#   Tick: advance time by 1, execute due schedules
#   Pause: schedule_name -> active = false
#   Resume: schedule_name -> active = true
#   Remove: schedule_name -> deleted
#   Execution: func(*args) called when interval elapsed
#   Error handling: errors logged, schedule continues
#
#
# === Search Protocol ===
#
#   Index Operations:
#     add_document(doc_id, text) -> indexed
#     remove_document(doc_id) -> deindexed
#
#   Search Operations:
#     search(query, limit) -> [{doc_id, score}, ...]
#     Scoring: TF-IDF (Term Frequency * Inverse Document Frequency)
#     Ranking: descending by score
#
#   Query Syntax:
#     Simple: 'hello world' (OR semantics)
#     Phrase: '"exact phrase"'
#     Boolean: 'hello AND world NOT spam'
#     Grouped: '(hello OR hi) AND world'
#
#   Tokenization:
#     Lowercase normalization
#     Alphanumeric characters only
#     Whitespace and punctuation as delimiters
#
#
# === Permission Protocol ===
#
#   Role Definition:
#     define_role(name, [permissions]) -> stored
#     Permissions: arbitrary strings (e.g., 'read', 'write', 'admin')
#
#   Role Assignment:
#     assign_role(user_id, role) -> bool (success)
#     revoke_role(user_id, role) -> bool (success)
#     Users can have multiple roles
#
#   Permission Check:
#     check(user_id, permission) -> bool (granted)
#     Checks all assigned roles for the permission
#     Deny-by-default: unrecognized users/permissions -> False
#     All checks logged for auditing
#
#   Queries:
#     get_permissions(user_id) -> set of all permissions
#     get_user_roles(user_id) -> list of assigned roles
#     get_all_roles() -> list of defined roles
#
#
# ============================================================================
# SECTION 18: RUNTIME INVARIANTS
# ============================================================================
#
# ScarabDrum Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: beat() always returns a dict with 'position' and 'velocity' keys
#   INVARIANT: get_state() returns a deep copy (modifying it doesn't affect drum)
#   INVARIANT: reset() returns drum to exact initial state
#   INVARIANT: set_mode() only accepts 'standard', 'extended', 'turbo'
#   INVARIANT: State is consistent across sequential beat() calls
#
# BTree Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: All keys maintain sorted order at all times
#   INVARIANT: Tree height is O(log n) where n = number of entries
#   INVARIANT: Every non-root node has at least ceil(order/2) keys
#   INVARIANT: Root has at least 1 key (when non-empty)
#   INVARIANT: All leaves are at the same depth
#   INVARIANT: search(k) after insert(k, v) always returns v
#   INVARIANT: delete(k) followed by search(k) returns None
#
# BloomFilter Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: If check(x) returns False, x was never added
#   INVARIANT: If add(x) was called, check(x) always returns True
#   INVARIANT: False positive rate <= configured FPR for capacity
#   INVARIANT: Bit array size is fixed after initialization
#   INVARIANT: Hash count is optimal for configured capacity and FPR
#
# ConsistentHash Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: get_node(k) returns consistent result if nodes unchanged
#   INVARIANT: Adding a node redistributes minimal keys
#   INVARIANT: Removing a node only affects keys mapped to that node
#   INVARIANT: Virtual nodes ensure even distribution across physical nodes
#   INVARIANT: Empty ring returns None for any key
#
# EventStream Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Sequence numbers are strictly monotonically increasing
#   INVARIANT: Events are never reordered within the stream
#   INVARIANT: consume() never returns the same event twice to same consumer
#   INVARIANT: replay() returns events in original order
#   INVARIANT: Stream size never exceeds max_size
#   INVARIANT: clear() resets sequence counter to 0
#
# PubSubBroker Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Published message delivered to all current subscribers of topic
#   INVARIANT: Unsubscribed consumers don't receive new messages
#   INVARIANT: receive() removes messages from inbox (at-most-once delivery)
#   INVARIANT: Message IDs are monotonically increasing
#   INVARIANT: Topic deletion removes all messages for that topic
#
# FullTextIndex Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: add_document followed by search for contained term returns document
#   INVARIANT: remove_document followed by search returns no results for that doc
#   INVARIANT: Search results are sorted by TF-IDF score (descending)
#   INVARIANT: Vocabulary size equals number of unique terms across all documents
#   INVARIANT: get_documents_containing returns exact set of docs with that term
#
# PermissionGuard Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: check() returns False for undefined users (deny-by-default)
#   INVARIANT: check() returns False for undefined permissions
#   INVARIANT: assign_role returns False for undefined roles
#   INVARIANT: All check() calls are logged to check_log
#   INVARIANT: get_permissions returns union of all assigned roles' permissions
#   INVARIANT: revoke_role removes only the specified role, not others
#
# TokenVault Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Generated tokens are unique (never reused)
#   INVARIANT: Revoked tokens always fail validation
#   INVARIANT: Rotated tokens: old revoked, new valid
#   INVARIANT: get_active_count + get_revoked_count = total generated
#   INVARIANT: validate() for non-existent token returns reason='not_found'
#
# AuditTrail Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Sequence numbers are monotonically increasing
#   INVARIANT: Entries are never modified after creation
#   INVARIANT: query() returns entries in reverse chronological order
#   INVARIANT: get_total() equals len(entries)
#   INVARIANT: clear() resets both entries and sequence counter
#   INVARIANT: Total entries never exceeds max_entries
#
# JobRunner Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Job status transitions: pending -> running -> completed | failed
#   INVARIANT: Cancelled jobs never execute
#   INVARIANT: Completed jobs have non-None result
#   INVARIANT: Failed jobs have non-None error
#   INVARIANT: Retry count never exceeds max_retries
#
# CronScheduler Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Tick counter is monotonically increasing
#   INVARIANT: Paused schedules never execute
#   INVARIANT: Execution log entries match actual executions
#   INVARIANT: Run count equals number of successful executions
#   INVARIANT: Removed schedules are permanently deleted
#
# Heartbeat Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: beat() sets status to 'healthy'
#   INVARIANT: Missing beats beyond timeout sets status to 'unhealthy'
#   INVARIANT: get_healthy() + get_unhealthy() + unknown <= total services
#   INVARIANT: Tick counter is monotonically increasing
#   INVARIANT: beat_count is monotonically increasing per service
#
# IncidentManager Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Incident IDs are unique and sequential
#   INVARIANT: Status transitions follow: open -> investigating -> mitigated -> resolved -> closed
#   INVARIANT: Timeline is append-only
#   INVARIANT: Created incidents always start in 'open' status
#   INVARIANT: get_open() returns incidents in 'open' or 'investigating' status
#
# TelemetryCollector Invariants:
#   INVARIANT: Collected values are never modified after storage
#   INVARIANT: aggregate('mean') = sum(values) / len(values)
#   INVARIANT: aggregate('sum') = sum(all values across all sources)
#   INVARIANT: aggregate('min') = minimum value across all sources
#   INVARIANT: aggregate('max') = maximum value across all sources
#   INVARIANT: collection_count equals total number of collect() calls
#
#
