# ScarabDrum Lifecycle:
#
#   Phase 1: Initialization
#     - Constructor called with configuration parameters
#     - Internal data structures allocated
#     - Default values applied for omitted configuration
#     - Component registered with monitoring (if available)
#     - Initialization event emitted
#
#   Phase 2: Configuration
#     - Runtime configuration applied
#     - Dependencies injected
#     - Event handlers registered
#     - Metrics collection started
#     - Health check registered
#
#   Phase 3: Active Operation
#     - Component processes requests/data
#     - State maintained and updated
#     - Events emitted for state changes
#     - Metrics collected continuously
#     - Health status reported via heartbeat
#
#   Phase 4: Graceful Shutdown
#     - Stop accepting new requests
#     - Complete in-flight operations
#     - Flush pending data/events
#     - Release resources (connections, memory)
#     - Emit shutdown event
#     - Deregister from monitoring
#
#   Phase 5: Cleanup
#     - Final resource deallocation
#     - Persistent state saved (if applicable)
#     - Temporary files removed
#     - Component reference cleared
